From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dplayx: lobby RegisterApplication, UnregisterApplication, EnumLocalApplications, RunApplication, lobby messages, ConnectEx

- RegisterApplication / UnregisterApplication (A and W): the application is
  a subkey of HKLM\Software\Microsoft\DirectPlay\Applications (Guid, File,
  Path, CommandLine, CurrentDirectory, descriptions); parameter errors, and
  DPERR_UNKNOWNAPPLICATION for an unknown guid.
- EnumLocalApplications (Unicode, and the ANSI one no longer leaks keys).
- RunApplication (Unicode): shares the code with the ANSI one, which no
  longer crashes for an application that is not registered
  (DPERR_UNKNOWNAPPLICATION), quotes the program name, and sets the receive
  event for the messages of the application.
- Send/ReceiveLobbyMessage and SetLobbyMessageEvent: two queues (client to
  application, application to client) in the shared storage of the DLL so
  that they work across processes, with the events duplicated into the
  process that sends; DPERR_NOMESSAGES, DPERR_BUFFERTOOSMALL (the message
  stays), DPERR_BUFFERTOOLARGE (4096 bytes), DPERR_NOTLOBBIED.
- ConnectEx: initializes the service provider from the address of the
  connection settings, opens the session, uses the ANSI interface whatever
  was asked for, and gives no object when it fails.

